<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

{% include "head.liquid" %}

<body>
  {% include "header.liquid" %}

  <article class="container post">

    <header class="post-header">
      <h1 class="post-title">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>
    </header>

    {% comment %}
      The intro's source list. `ref.liquid` cannot hand the entries up in a variable: cobalt renders
      a document and its layout against separate globals (measured). So each call site leaves its
      `<li>` inline inside an HTML comment fenced by `<!--ref-->`, and the split below pulls them
      out -- even chunks = page, odd = entry. A page with no references splits into one chunk.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign ref_chunks = page.content | split: "<!--ref-->" %}
    <div class="post-content">
      {% for ref_chunk in ref_chunks %}{% assign ref_odd = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 %}{% if ref_odd == 0 %}{{ ref_chunk }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% assign ref_chunk_n = ref_chunks | size %}
      {% if ref_chunk_n > 1 %}
      <ol class="ref-list" aria-label="Sources for this introduction">
        {% for ref_chunk in ref_chunks %}{% assign ref_odd = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 %}{% if ref_odd == 1 %}{{ ref_chunk | remove_first: "<!--" | remove_first: "-->" }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </ol>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      Sections carry their own color, because maturity varies wildly inside a hub. Only `featured`
      is set by hand. The archive band lives on this page rather than in a graveyard, so someone
      searching for a dead crate finds out here that it is dead instead of finding nothing.
    {% endcomment %}

    {% for hub in site.data.topics %}{% if hub.id == page.data.hub %}
    <nav class="hub-bar" aria-label="Shelves on this page">
      {% for section in hub.sections %}
      {% assign color = section.color %}
      <a class="hub-bar-item" href="#{{ section.id | escape }}">
        <span class="seg swatch-{{ section.color | escape }}"></span>
        <span class="hub-bar-label">{{ section.title | escape }}
          <span class="hub-bar-verdict {{ section.color | escape }}">{% include "verdict.liquid" %}</span></span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}

    {% assign crates = site.data.crates_generated | sort: 'score' | reverse %}
    {% for hub in site.data.topics %}
    {% if hub.id == page.data.hub %}
    {% for section in hub.sections %}
    {% assign n_featured = 0 %}{% assign n_listed = 0 %}{% assign n_watch = 0 %}{% assign n_archive = 0 %}
    {% for crate in crates %}{% if crate.topics contains section.id %}{% if crate.tier == 'featured' %}{% assign n_featured = n_featured | plus: 1 %}{% elsif crate.tier == 'listed' %}{% assign n_listed = n_listed | plus: 1 %}{% elsif crate.tier == 'watch' %}{% assign n_watch = n_watch | plus: 1 %}{% elsif crate.tier == 'archive' %}{% assign n_archive = n_archive | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

    {% comment %} `--verdict` is scoped to `.shelf-head`, not the section: a shelf color is a claim
      about the problem space, never about an entry. On the section wrapper it ran a 4px rail down
      the side of all 80 of them. {% endcomment %}
    <section class="shelf" id="{{ section.id | escape }}">
      <div class="shelf-head shelf-head-{{ section.color | escape }}">
        <h2 class="shelf-title">
          <a href="#{{ section.id | escape }}">{{ section.title | escape }}</a>
          {% assign color = section.color %}<span class="shelf-status status-{{ section.color | escape }}">{% include "verdict.liquid" %}</span>
        </h2>
        {% comment %}
          A blurb cannot hold an include, so its markers are bare `[n]` and its sources are data.
          `section.sources` is read inside `{% if %}` and never in the `assign`: cobalt errors on an
          unknown index there, and most sections have no `sources` key. The markup comes from
          ref.liquid's `ref_entry_id` mode, so the two source lists cannot drift apart.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% assign prose_sources = "" %}{% if section.sources %}{% assign prose_sources = section.sources %}{% endif %}
        {% assign prose_key = section.id %}
        <p class="shelf-blurb">{% assign prose = section.blurb %}{% include "prose.liquid" %}</p>
        {% if section.sources %}
        <ol class="ref-list" aria-label="Sources for this shelf">
          {% for source in section.sources %}
          {% capture ref_entry_id %}src-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index }}{% endcapture %}
          {% assign ref_src = source.src %}{% assign ref_url = source.url %}
          {% assign ref_date = "" %}{% if source.date %}{% assign ref_date = source.date %}{% endif %}
          {% assign ref_note = "" %}{% if source.note %}{% assign ref_note = source.note %}{% endif %}
          {% include "ref.liquid" %}
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {% comment %} Gated on what is alive, not on the section's total: a shelf whose only entries
        are archived is the shelf that most needs someone to suggest a replacement. {% endcomment %}
      {% assign n_live = n_featured | plus: n_listed | plus: n_watch %}
      {% if n_live == 0 %}
      <p class="shelf-empty">
        {% if n_archive > 0 %}Everything we know of here is dead &mdash; if something has replaced it,
        {% else %}Nothing listed here yet &mdash;
        {% endif %}
        <a href="https://github.com/anowell/are-we-learning-yet/issues/new?template=report.md">suggest something</a>.
      </p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if n_featured > 0 %}
      <div class="band band-featured">
        {% for crate in crates %}
        {% if crate.topics contains section.id and crate.tier == 'featured' %}
        {% include "crate.liquid" %}
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if n_listed > 0 %}
      <div class="band band-listed">
        {% for crate in crates %}
        {% if crate.topics contains section.id and crate.tier == 'listed' %}
        {% include "crate.liquid" %}
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if n_watch > 0 %}
      <details class="band band-watch">
        <summary>New &amp; experimental ({{ n_watch }})</summary>
        <p class="band-note">Collected, but not clearing the
          <a href="/about/">published listing bar</a> &mdash; too new, too quiet, or with no use
          by anyone but its author that we can see. Plenty of good software is here, some of it
          years old: this says what we can measure, not what it is worth.</p>
        {% for crate in crates %}
        {% if crate.topics contains section.id and crate.tier == 'watch' %}
        {% include "crate.liquid" %}
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </details>
      {% endif %}

      {% if n_archive > 0 %}
      <details class="band band-archive">
        <summary>Archive ({{ n_archive }})</summary>
        <p class="band-note">Kept so you stop looking for them. Archives are computed on every
          build and reverse themselves if the reason clears. Where a human has named the reason
          or a replacement, it cites the public issue behind that.</p>
        {% for crate in crates %}
        {% if crate.topics contains section.id and crate.tier == 'archive' %}
        {% include "crate.liquid" %}
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </section>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

  </article>
  {% include "footer.liquid" %}

</body>

</html>
